# No builds unless requested

Do **not** run the compiler, linker, CMake configure/build, `make`/`ninja`, or packaging steps unless the user explicitly asks to build, compile, or confirm the project builds. Other rules that mention CMake or new sources do **not** override this.

## Verify without building

After editing code, catch syntax and obvious mistakes with:

- IDE/linter diagnostics (`ReadLints` / language server)
- Project MCP or other static-analysis tools when available
- A short review of the changed files and their call sites

A full compile is **not** the default verification step.

## When a build is appropriate

Build only when the user clearly asks for it — for example “build”, “compile”, “reconfigure cmake”, or “check that it builds” — or when they request packaging/install work that cannot be done without a build.
